+# Compact front corner continuity - 2026-10-10
+
+Requirements: CG08 (owner-marked front/fender/hood surfaces must join), CG07 (rounded upper corner), CG01-CG06, GL01-GL06, V06/R01/Q01. This is a cosmetic repair to the actual shared Compact model used in Garage and driving.
+
+The former side skin ended at z=-2.08m with an independent width taper, the hood used a different outline, and a separately closed rounded nose box overlapped both. Rounding that box did not fix their incompatible boundaries. The box is replaced by a bowed front face and two continuous cubic corner patches whose tangents meet the fascia and side panel. The hood rim, front corners and fender use the same boundary points and matching 24/40/24 subdivisions; the hood side has matching 24 fender stations. A 30mm rolled upper profile softens the front and side transition into the hood. A front underpan closes the lower skin.
+
+The dark fascia and thin amber corner indicators now follow that same body curve, with their backs embedded in the steel. The previous thick rectangular fascia back wall and floating indicator boxes are removed. Each fitting is constructed as one combined mesh. Front arch lips follow the revised side width. Body/accent painting, functional headlight/brake behavior, wheel transforms, the owner's taller/thinner mirrors, rear/roof joints and ruled windshield are retained. Canonical physics, collision, race acceptance, camera controls, menus and other car geometry are untouched.
+
+Runtime uses original coachwork v3: **50 native resources, 711101 bytes** (46 coachwork and four glazing/seal surfaces). Prior v1/v2 assets remain preserved. Four joined front resources replace six independent nose-box resources. Eight existing body/hood/front-arch resources have revised geometry; the other **38 shared resources, including all 14 mirror surfaces and all cabin/rear/roof/glass surfaces, have exact v2 array parity**. New-directory resource UIDs change binary hashes even when arrays remain identical. V3 manifest pins actual SHA-256 hashes and sizes; its PROVENANCE.md and licenses/ASSETS.md retain original fictional-asset provenance. No external mesh, texture, image-generation service, screenshot pixels or runtime API was added.
+
+Changed files: `game/vehicle/compact_coachwork.gd`, `compact_detail.gd`, `car_visual.gd`; expected native-resource count in `game/tests/test_garage_studio.gd`; new `game/tests/test_compact_front_join.gd` and UID; the v3 native resources, manifest and provenance; this document and scoped status/plan/license entries. [Task-only binary/text Git checkpoint](evidence/compact-front-join-2026-10-10/scoped-change.patch) excludes unrelated workspace changes and preserves the preceding Garage work.
+
+Actual engine commands use pinned Godot **4.7.2.stable.official.ed1daf0bf** through `powershell -NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File scripts/dev.ps1`, with normal Windows engine log/certificate access. Actual-app fixtures disable API requests and redirect records/library/cloud paths to isolated storage.
+
+| Actual command | Actual result |
+| --- | --- |
+| `-Action TestScript -ScriptPath res://tests/bake_compact_coachwork.gd` | Final 50 meshes / 711101 bytes, exit 0 |
+| `-Action Import` | Script-class/cache refresh succeeds; resolves initial Garage fixture startup failure on concurrently added `GrassBirds` |
+| `-Action TestScript -ScriptPath res://tests/test_compact_front_join.gd -Graphical` | Final **116 checks, zero failures**: bidirectional actual baked edge comparisons, tangent/lighting continuity, 38 exact prior-array comparisons, wheels and five actual-app captures |
+| `-Action TestScript -ScriptPath res://tests/test_garage_studio.gd -Graphical` | Final **75 checks, zero failures**: exact source/bake arrays for all 50 resources, finite UV geometry, liveries, studio/driving glass isolation, wheel transforms and batching |
+| `-Action TestScript -ScriptPath res://tests/test_compact_joints.gd -Graphical` | **368 checks, zero failures**: earlier rear/roof joins, ruled glass, wheels and native views |
+| `-Action TestScript -ScriptPath res://tests/test_garage_livery.gd -Graphical` | **115 checks, zero failures**: saved colors, picker/reset/failure handling and driving application |
+| `-Action TestVehicleBatch` | Final **35 checks, zero failures**, exact all-car source/batched geometry and bounds; Compact 879 parts -> 47 batched meshes / 95936 triangles |
+| `-Action TestSuspension` | **59 checks, zero failures**, existing presentation behavior retained |
+| `-Action TestHeadlights` | Final **81 checks, zero failures**; initial run stopped on temporary `scrape.wav` load failure during concurrent audio work, unchanged retry passes |
+| `-Action TestScript -ScriptPath res://tests/test_script_parse.gd` | **476 scripts, zero failures** in the current shared workspace |
+| `C:/Users/ville/AppData/Local/Android/Sdk/platform-tools/adb.exe devices -l` | OPD2403 OnePlus Pad2 / f0ba474a attached; **no phone attached**. Bare adb unavailable on PATH; sandboxed invocation could not create its configuration directory, normal-access read succeeds |
+| Scoped whitespace and reverse-apply checkpoint checks | Pass |
+
+Final maximum hood/front/corner edge discrepancy is **0.000000377m** (0.000377mm); hood/fender discrepancy **0.000000119m**; the face/corner and fender/corner edges are exact. Actual shared lighting normals differ by at most **0.093 degrees** at face/corner and **4.602 degrees** at fender/corner, including finite-difference fillet endpoints, under the retained eight-degree visual continuity bound. An intermediate hood-edge fixture accidentally included interior crown points after adding the roll; selecting its actual endpoint samples fixes the fixture, retaining the same 0.2mm bidirectional tolerance. No failing product assertion was removed.
+
+Native evidence inspected: [right corner](evidence/compact-front-join-2026-10-10/corner-right-1280.png), [left corner](evidence/compact-front-join-2026-10-10/corner-left-1280.png), [low angle](evidence/compact-front-join-2026-10-10/corner-low-1280.png), [hood join](evidence/compact-front-join-2026-10-10/hood-join-1280.png), [normal Garage view](evidence/compact-front-join-2026-10-10/garage-1280.png). Close-ups use only a fixture inspection target/FOV; shipping Garage controls stay unchanged.
+
+Final studio model: **95936 triangles, 47 batched meshes, 65956 UV vertices**. One desktop construction observation is315.826ms; RTX3090 Compatibility SubViewport CPUmedian0.711ms/GPUmedian0.474ms during concurrent graphical fixtures. These are desktop observations, not phone FPS, whole-app timing or an AAA-quality acceptance claim. No physical-device test, Android export/install, full Validate, canonical physics regression, backend deployment or production action was performed. Remaining acceptance: owner close-up shape review and tablet/phone presentation/performance. Restart/rebuild the client to load v3 baked resources.
